{{!-- A slides single — the DECK PLAYER in PRESENT MODE: no
navbar, no footer — the slide owns the viewport, and the
topbar's ✕ is the way back (Esc does the same outside
fullscreen). The site chrome is hidden by CSS on the post's own
tag-hash-slides body class (slides/_frame.css) — a layout
declaration can't do it, because this file is a PARTIAL and
express-hbs only honours the layout named by the top-level
template (post.hbs). Built on the NS Slides player grammar
(../../slides in the monorepo):

  · the slide is a FIXED logical canvas (1280×720) scaled with a
    CSS transform to fit the stage — never reflowed, so a slide
    lays out identically on every screen (deck.js sets the scale)
  · the canvas is the NSDS LIGHT surface (the thumbnail
    treatment: near-white, blueprint grid, navy ink), letterboxed
    on near-black like a cinema so the slide pops
  · click / → / Space forward, ← back, a progress bar, a counter,
    fullscreen, and a toggle that folds the filmstrip away

The post's content IS the deck: every divider card (---) ends a
slide. The rail is a real FILMSTRIP — deck.js clones each slide
into a miniature at thumbnail scale.

With JS off nothing is hidden: the frame falls back to a normal
scrolling article (the topbar stays, so ✕ still leads out).
Member gating is Ghost's own post access — outside the audience
{{access}} is false and the stage shows the locked cover
instead. Context: post. --}}

<main id="site-main" class="deck-frame {{post_class}}" data-deck>

    <header class="deck-topbar">
        <a class="deck-topbar-close" href="{{@site.url}}/slides/" data-deck-close aria-label="{{t "Close the deck"}}">
            {{> "icons/close"}}
        </a>
        <div class="deck-topbar-title">
            <strong>{{title}}</strong>
            {{#match visibility "!=" "public"}}
                <span class="chip deck-chip-members">{{> "icons/lock"}} {{t "Members"}}</span>
            {{/match}}
            {{> "duration-chip" chipClass="chip deck-topbar-chip"}}
        </div>
        {{#if access}}
            <div class="deck-topbar-actions" data-deck-controls hidden>
                <span class="deck-keys" aria-hidden="true" title="{{t "Use ← and → to move between slides"}}"><kbd>←</kbd><kbd>→</kbd></span>
                <span class="deck-counter" data-deck-counter aria-live="polite"></span>
                <button class="deck-btn" type="button" data-deck-prev aria-label="{{t "Previous slide"}}">{{> "icons/arrow-left"}}</button>
                <button class="deck-btn" type="button" data-deck-next aria-label="{{t "Next slide"}}">{{> "icons/arrow-right"}}</button>
                <button class="deck-btn" type="button" data-deck-rail-toggle aria-label="{{t "Show or hide the slide list"}}" aria-pressed="true">{{> "icons/list-icon"}}</button>
                <button class="deck-btn" type="button" data-deck-full aria-label="{{t "Fullscreen"}}">{{> "icons/expand"}}</button>
            </div>
        {{/if}}
    </header>

    {{#if access}}

        <div class="deck-body">
            {{!-- The filmstrip: deck.js fills it with one mini
            per slide — the same content, thumbnail scale. --}}
            <aside class="deck-rail" data-deck-rail hidden>
                <ol class="deck-nav" data-deck-nav></ol>
            </aside>

            <div class="deck-stage" data-deck-stage>
                <div class="deck-canvas-box" data-deck-box>
                    <div class="deck-canvas" data-deck-canvas>
                        <section class="gh-content deck-source" data-deck-source>
                            {{content}}
                        </section>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <span class="deck-progress" aria-hidden="true"><i data-deck-progress></i></span>
            </div>
        </div>

    {{else}}

        {{!-- The locked cover on the same cinema stage: the deck
        is real, the door is not open. Ghost decided (post
        visibility vs this visitor); this just says so. --}}
        <div class="deck-body is-locked">
            <div class="deck-stage">
                <div class="deck-locked">
                    {{#if feature_image}}
                        <img class="deck-locked-cover" src="{{img_url feature_image size="l"}}" alt="" loading="lazy" aria-hidden="true" />
                    {{/if}}
                    <div class="deck-locked-panel">
                        <span class="deck-locked-badge" aria-hidden="true">{{> "icons/lock"}}</span>
                        {{#match visibility "paid"}}
                            <h2>{{t "This deck is for paid members"}}</h2>
                            <p>{{t "Upgrade to open every slide — and every other members-only deck, lesson and issue on the site."}}</p>
                            <div class="deck-locked-actions">
                                <a class="btn btn-lg" href="{{@site.url}}/membership/">{{> "icons/star"}} {{t "See membership"}}</a>
                                <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="{{@site.url}}/signin/">{{t "Already a member? Sign in"}}</a>
                            </div>
                        {{else}}
                            <h2>{{t "This deck is for members"}}</h2>
                            <p>{{t "Join free to open every slide — it takes one email and five seconds, and you get the weekly letter with it."}}</p>
                            <div class="deck-locked-actions">
                                <a class="btn btn-lg" href="{{@site.url}}/signup/">{{> "icons/mail"}} {{t "Join free"}}</a>
                                <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="{{@site.url}}/signin/">{{t "Already a member? Sign in"}}</a>
                            </div>
                        {{/match}}
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

    {{/if}}

</main>
